.TH ARMORY\-READ 1 2026-10-25 "blocktools 0.1.0" "blocktools manual"
.SH NAME
armory\-read \- Armory (PyBtcWallet) `.wallet` \-> {"wif","chain_index"} per stored address
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
armory\-read < (password line, then Armory .wallet) \-> {"wif","chain_index"} per address
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
(uncompressed keys, as Armory uses). Output CONTAINS SECRETS. Pipe to key\-to\-addresses
\-\-chain btc (addresses) or tx\-sign (keys).
stdin: line 1 = password (empty for an unencrypted wallet), rest = the wallet file.
Thin wrapper around blocktools_secrets::armory; every key reproduces the stored public key.
.SH WARNING
DANGEROUS: use at your own risk. Code that handles keys and signs transactions should always be read and audited by you before you trust it with real funds. Used incorrectly, it can destroy your money.
.br
Used incorrectly (wrong address, huge fee, lost keys, wrong chain) you lose funds; verify every transaction.
.br
It opens hostile wallet files and extracts secrets: run it only sealed and offline (./blocktools run).
.br
Unit tests are evidence, not a substitute for your own review. See docs/SECURITY.md.
.SH SEE ALSO
blocktools(7), docs/SECURITY.md, recipes/README.md
